    ("the hook stays silent on a passing change", dict(runs=one([("notes/a.txt", "a\n", "write")], stdin=HOOK), script=["check", "--hook"], expect=lambda o: is_silent(o[-1]))),
]


# (file, old text, new text, what the mutant breaks); each old text occurs exactly once.
# Rule lines in scripts/risk-paths and entries of CHECKS are covered by the data-driven cases;
# deleting one is a reviewed change to the rules, not a silent break, and is not listed here.
# check's crash handler in --hook is not listed: no input the cases can build crashes the hook.
# check-upkeep's cell-count and parse branches are not listed: without them the row crashes the
# script, which fails it just the same.
